>/dev/rmt/0 /solaris/file1 /solaris/file2 ...", verified it using "tar tvf
>/dev/rmt/0" and everything are there as expected.

There's a big problem with using "absolute" path names, i.e. those starting
with a '/'....

  However when I extracted
>these files on the Alpha 600 running tru64 Unix V4.0f with this command "tar
>xvf /dev/rmt0h", it gave me an error saying "No space left on device".
>Note, before doing this, I already cd it to a directory where I want to put
>it.

You cd'd to something like /bigfs/users/le/solaris, but then tar proceded
to create /solaris/file1 /solaris/file2 ....  I bet you did this as root and
have filled up your root partition.

I think tar has an option to override or prepend a string to files being
restored.  Find that or just go back to Solaris and do

# cd /
# tar .... solaris/file1 solaris/file2 ...

And clean up your root partition on the Tru64 system!

